equipment manufactured under the CNH Industrial family of brands, as well as equipment from various other manufacturers. The company offers agricultural equipment, including machinery and attachments for use in the production of food, fiber, feed grain, feedstock, and renewable energy; and home and garden applications, as well as maintenance of commercial, residential, and government properties. It also provides construction equipment, such as heavy construction machinery, light industrial machinery for commercial and residential construction, and road and highway construction machinery. In addition, the company offers repair and maintenance services that include warranty repairs, off-site and on-site repair services, scheduling off-season maintenance services, and notifying customers of periodic service requirements; and training programs to customers, as well as sells maintenance and replacement parts. Further, the company rents equipment; and provides ancillary equipment support services, such as equipment transportation, global positioning system signal subscriptions and other precision farming products, farm data management products, and finance and insurance products. It operates in Colorado, Idaho, Iowa, Kansas, Minnesota, Nebraska, North Dakota, South Dakota, Wisconsin, and Wyoming, the United States; Bulgaria, Germany, Romania, and Ukraine, Europe; and New South Wales, South Australia, and Victoria, and Australia. The company was founded in 1980 and is headquartered in West Fargo, North Dakota.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Bryan J. Knutson | President, CEO & Director | Age 47 | Compensation: $960,841 (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $779K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Titan Machinery Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $528M market cap on $2.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 18% against a 9% cost of capital, a 9-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, and 18% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 11% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins 9% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 239% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.387738131236771},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Industrials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Titan Machinery (TITN) Stock Is Up 7.0% Today Without Company News","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/titan-machinery-titn-stock-7-154514293.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795794314.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Titan (TITN) Q3 2027 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/titan-titn-q3-2027-earnings-185932000.html","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795547368.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Titan Machinery (TITN) Stock Is Down 9.7% Today: Revenue Miss, Europe Outlook Cut","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/titan-machinery-titn-stock-down-170030785.html","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795539630.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.586,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Titan Machinery Inc (TITN) (Q3 2027) Earnings Call Highlights: Margin Expansion and Inventory ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/titan-machinery-inc-titn-q3-162117155.html","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795537277.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.718,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Titan Machinery (TITN) Q3 Earnings: